---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const title = "What Skills Do You Have? Interview Answer for Freshers in India";
const seoTitle = "What Skills Do You Have? Interview Answer for Freshers";
const description = "What skills do you have? How freshers in India can answer with three matched skills and proof, what interviewers check and mistakes to avoid.";
const seoDescription = "What skills do you have? How freshers in India can answer with three matched skills and proof, what interviewers check and mistakes to avoid.";
const canonical = "https://futurecareerschool.com/blog/interviews/what-skills-do-you-have-interview-answer-india/";
const publishedDateISO = "2026-10-30";
const publishedDateLabel = "30 October 2026";
const authorName = "Shivanshi Sehgal";
const authorUrl = "https://futurecareerschool.com/about/shivanshi-sehgal/";
const authorRole = "Career researcher and writer";

const faqItems = [
  {
    "q": "What skills do you have? How should I answer?",
    "a": "Name three matching skills with one proof each and one skill you are learning."
  },
  {
    "q": "How many skills should I list?",
    "a": "Three, matched to the notice."
  },
  {
    "q": "What if I do not have all the skills?",
    "a": "Say what you are learning and how."
  },
  {
    "q": "Should I mention soft skills?",
    "a": "Yes, if you can give evidence."
  },
  {
    "q": "How long should the answer be?",
    "a": "About a minute."
  },
  {
    "q": "Can I use college projects as proof?",
    "a": "Yes, if they are real and you can explain them."
  },
  {
    "q": "Will AI replace this question?",
    "a": "The question stays. Proof matters more."
  },
  {
    "q": "How do I avoid sounding rehearsed?",
    "a": "Know the facts and speak plainly."
  }
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  seoTitle={seoTitle}
  seoDescription={seoDescription}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="interviews"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    To answer what skills you have, pick the three skills the notice asks for that you can prove, give one line of evidence for each and finish with the skill you are building, because a matched and proven short list beats a long list of adjectives.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Short answer:</strong> Read the notice, choose three matching skills and attach one proof to each. Say what you are learning next.</li>
      <li><strong>Who is asking:</strong> The recruiter checks fit with the notice, the manager checks depth and the owner checks whether you will learn quickly.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> The decisions that unlock high income opportunities come from finished work in one lane. Proof you can show supports an earlier path to financial freedom.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

      <p>Want a second opinion on this decision? <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-coaching-for-freshers/">career coaching for freshers</a> is the direct route.</p>

  <p>
    This answer is about fit with this job. The question is not asking for everything you can do, but for what you can do that this role needs.
  </p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li><a href="#match">Match to the notice</a></li>
      <li><a href="#shape">Answer shape</a></li>
      <li><a href="#samples">Sample answers</a></li>
      <li><a href="#routes">Routes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#reality">Pay, growth and AI</a></li>
      <li><a href="#learn">Learn it cheaply</a></li>
      <li><a href="#money">Money</a></li>
      <li><a href="#checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gate3">The 3 Gates</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mistakes">Expensive mistakes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#next-step">What to do next</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="match">How to match your skills to the job notice</h2>
  <p>
    Do this before every interview.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Step</th>
          <th>What to do</th>
          <th>Output</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Highlight repeated words</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Mark skills and tools that appear more than once</td>
          <td data-label="Output">A list of five to eight items</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Mark what you can prove</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Tick only items with a real example</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Three to four items</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Attach one proof each</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">A project, task or result</td>
          <td data-label="Output">One line of evidence per skill</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Pick one learning skill</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Choose a gap you are working on</td>
          <td data-label="Output">A line about your next step</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="shape">The shape of a strong answer</h2>
  <p>
    Keep it under a minute and spoken in plain words.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Part</th>
          <th>What to say</th>
          <th>Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Skill one with proof</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to say">Name it and give evidence</td>
          <td data-label="Example">I use spreadsheets well. I built a sales tracker for a shop with weekly totals</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Skill two with proof</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to say">Name it and give evidence</td>
          <td data-label="Example">I write clearly. I wrote the college newsletter for a year</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>Skill three with proof</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to say">Name it and give evidence</td>
          <td data-label="Example">I learn tools quickly. I learned a design tool in a short time and built a poster set</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Part"><strong>What you are building</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to say">Name a gap honestly</td>
          <td data-label="Example">I am improving my data skills through an online course and practice sets</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="samples">Sample answers for three kinds of fresher</h2>
  <p>
    Adapt the details to your own life. Never claim a skill you cannot show.
  </p>
  <div class="faq-accordion">
    <details open><summary>Commerce graduate applying for accounts</summary><div class="faq-a">I have three skills that match your notice. First, accounting software: I kept the books for a small shop and reconciled them monthly. Second, spreadsheets: I built a GST summary with lookups. Third, careful communication: I wrote the follow-up notes for pending invoices. I am now learning the tax portal in more depth.</div></details>
    <details><summary>Engineering graduate applying for a design role</summary><div class="faq-a">My strongest skills are CAD, basic analysis and reporting. I designed and analysed a small fixture for my final project and documented the assumptions. I am improving my knowledge of manufacturing standards.</div></details>
    <details><summary>Arts graduate applying for a content role</summary><div class="faq-a">I can research, write and edit. I researched and wrote twelve articles for a college magazine and edited the others. I am learning search basics and analytics.</div></details>
  </div>

  <h2 id="routes">Routes for what skills do you have, strongest growth first</h2>
  <p>
    These are rated for how far your own effort can scale beyond a salary. The ratings are judgement, not statistics.
  </p>
  <div class="route-grid">
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">01</span>
        <span class="chip chip--high">Scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>A small service built on the three skills you can prove, such as tracking, writing or design</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Skills with proof can be sold directly to people who need them.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Customers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Samples and testimonials.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Client hunting.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Add clients and associates.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">02</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Roles that match your three strongest skills</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Interviews go better when your skills match the notice.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Proof items.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Competition.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move to specialist roles.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">03</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Trainee and associate roles</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Employers expect to teach the rest.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Learning evidence.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Modest pay.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move to executive roles.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">04</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Internships that fill skill gaps</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Practice with feedback.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Work samples.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Low pay.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move to full-time roles.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">05</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Self-driven projects</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Show initiative.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Self.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Finished projects.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Needs discipline.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move to freelance work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">06</span>
        <span class="chip chip--low">Not so scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>A long list of adjectives</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">It sounds generic and cannot be checked.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Nobody.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Nothing.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Weak first impression.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Use matched skills with proof.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> a small service built on one skill you can prove, such as spreadsheets for local shops, design for small brands or writing for local firms, can start with samples and scale through repeat clients.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="reality">Pay, growth and AI for what skills do you have</h2>
  <p>
    Employers pay for skills they can see in action. The first skill is choosing proof that fits the notice.
  </p>
  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Freshers often list ten skills and prove none. Interviewers prefer three with evidence and an honest learning gap.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    Growth comes from stacking proven skills and learning what the role needs next. Candidates who learn quickly become trusted early.
  </p>
  <p>
    Drafting resumes and answers is easy with tools, which makes proof more valuable. Staged path: now, collect proof items; later, focus on judgement, communication and learning speed.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Better-fit option</th>
          <th>Why it can beat this one</th>
          <th>Catch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Better-fit option"><strong>Leadership and teamwork answers</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat this one">Handle other common questions.</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Need their own stories.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Better-fit option"><strong>Describing communication skills</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat this one">Deeper on one skill.</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Narrower scope.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="learn">Learn it cheaply and prove it</h2>
  <p>
    Free routes include free tool tutorials, college projects, volunteering and mock interviews with friends. Gather the proof items before you pay for any course.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judge any paid course by what you will finish, who reviews it and what the refund terms say in writing. Placement advertisements are not evidence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money: course fees and the 10 percent test</h2>
  <p>
    Our own working rule, from guiding families and not from a published study: keep a course or degree fee near a tenth of the family education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a caution that needs course-specific evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 1 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 10,000 for the main course and a fifth is Rs 20,000. Spend the rest on tools, practice and a reserve.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol for what skills do you have</h2>
  <p>
    Test the choice with <strong>The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</strong>: Biology, Context, Market and Survival. If one line stays empty, wait before you pay for anything.
  </p>
  <div class="protocol">
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Biology: which three skills does the notice ask for?</div>
        <p>Mark them in the notice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Context: time, money and support</div>
        <p>Count the practice rounds you can do.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Market: what proof do you have?</div>
        <p>Write one line per skill.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Survival: what survives AI?</div>
        <p>Learning speed and judgement outlast list making.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gate3">The 3 Gates: proof before commitment</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The 3 Gates</strong> ask whether your effort turns into work other people can check.
  </p>
  <div class="gates-block">
    <div class="gates-row">
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 1</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of reflection</span>
        <p>Mark three matching skills in the notice.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 2</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of research</span>
        <p>Write one proof for each.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 3</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of action</span>
        <p>Say the answer aloud in a minute.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="mistakes">Expensive mistakes with what skills do you have</h2>
  <div class="mistake-list">
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Listing many skills</div>
        <p>Choose three.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">No proof</div>
        <p>Attach evidence.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Claiming tools you cannot use</div>
        <p>Be honest.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Ignoring the notice</div>
        <p>Match it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Skipping the learning gap</div>
        <p>Name it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>
  <p>
    Mark three skills in the notice, write one proof for each and practise saying the answer in a minute.
  </p>
  <p>
    A specialist can look at your strengths, finances and goals with you. A sensible first step is <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-coaching-for-freshers/">career coaching for freshers</a>. The aim is a high-income skill portfolio and an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read also <a href="/blog/interviews/do-you-have-leadership-skills-interview-answer-india/">how to answer do you have leadership skills</a>, <a href="/blog/interviews/how-to-describe-your-communication-skills-in-an-interview-india/">how to describe your communication skills</a> and <a href="/blog/skills/transferable-skills-examples-and-how-to-show-them-india/">transferable skills</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="note-line">
     Interview styles differ by employer, so adapt the answer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQs on what skills do you have</h2>
  <div class="faq-accordion">
    {faqItems.map((item, index) => (
      <details open={index === 0}>
        <summary>{item.q}</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">{item.a}</div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <style>

    .check-list { display: grid; gap: 0.55rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    .lead-para {
      font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.65vw, 1.2rem);
      line-height: 1.85;
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82) !important;
      margin-top: 0 !important;
    }
    .lead-para strong { color: #fff; }

    .jump-nav {
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.05), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02));
      margin: 1.6rem 0 2rem;
    }
    .jump-nav__label {
      font-size: 11px !important;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.11em;
      color: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.96) !important;
      font-weight: 800;
      margin: 0 0 0.85rem !important;
    }
    .jump-nav__list {
      list-style: none !important;
      margin: 0 !important;
      padding: 0 !important;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.6rem 1rem;
    }
    .jump-nav__list li { margin: 0 !important; }
    .jump-nav__list a {
      display: block;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74);
      line-height: 1.55;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .jump-nav__list a:hover { color: #fff; }
    h2[id] { scroll-margin-top: 108px; }
    h2[id]:target { color: #fff6d7; }

    .key-takeaways {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      padding: 1.2rem 1.35rem 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 16px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.22);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 0% 0%, rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.1), transparent 60%),
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    }
    .key-takeaways__label {
      margin: 0 0 0.7rem !important;
      font-size: 11px !important;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.95) !important;
    }
    .key-takeaways ul {
      margin: 0 !important;
      padding-left: 1.15rem !important;
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .key-takeaways li {
      margin: 0 !important;
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82) !important;
      line-height: 1.7 !important;
      font-size: 15.5px;
    }

    .strand-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin: 1.4rem 0;
    }
    .strand-card {
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 1.15rem 1.1rem 1rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      border-top: 3px solid #2dd4bf;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    }
    .strand-card:nth-child(2) { border-top-color: #e5b84a; }
    .strand-card:nth-child(3) { border-top-color: #a78bfa; }
    .strand-card__name {
      font-family: "Sora", sans-serif;
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);
      margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    }
    .strand-card p {
      font-size: 14px !important;
      line-height: 1.7 !important;
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7) !important;
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem !important;
    }
    .strand-card__watch {
      padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: rgba(229, 184, 74, 0.08);
    }
    .strand-card__watch span {
      display: block;
      font-size: 10px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: #e5b84a;
      margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
    }

    .route-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .route-card {
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 1.2rem 1.15rem 1.1rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
